@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "osb.zendesk.integration"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk LRDCOM Integration
	Testing employee sync updates in Zendesk caused by changes in OSB via the LRDCOM org.

Setup:
	* I wait for "10" seconds

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View employee added to LRDCOM project
	New Liferay employees who are added to the LRDCOM org on OSB should not be added to the Zendesk Liferay.com org.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | liferay.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Liferay                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                            |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	And I assign a user the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "LRDCOM"
	And I assign a user the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" as a worker with the role "Sales" to the project with the code "LRDCOM"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the support organization "Liferay, Inc."
	Then the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Liferay.com"
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should have the "osb_lr_employee" tag
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the name "Liferay Employee1"